<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Simple or compound offer</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} has Ksh \({@ksh(P)@}\) to save for \({@n@}\) years.</p><p>Offer A: a SACCO fixed deposit paying \({@dd(r1)@}\%\) per annum simple interest.</p><p>Offer B: a bank account paying \({@r2@}\%\) per annum compound interest, added each year.</p><p>(a) Find the amount after \({@n@}\) years with offer A.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the amount after \({@n@}\) years with offer B, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Which offer gives more? [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Simple interest: \({@ksh(P)@} + \dfrac{{@ksh(P)@} \times {@dd(r1)@} \times {@n@}}{100} = {@ksh(P)@} + {@ksh(SI1)@} = {@ksh(S)@}\).</p><p>(b) Compound interest: \({@ksh(P)@} \times {@dd(m2)@}^{ {@n@} } = {@ksh(C)@}\)[[if test="not(integerp(C))"]], about Ksh \({@ksh(floor(C+1/2))@}\)[[/if]].</p><p>(c) [[if test="is(ky=1)"]]Offer A gives more, by Ksh \({@ksh(S-C)@}\).[[else]]Offer B gives more, by Ksh \({@ksh(C-S)@}\).[[/if]]</p><p>Simple interest adds the same sum every year; compound interest multiplies by the same number every year. A higher simple rate can win over a few years, but over a longer time compound interest pulls ahead.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: [P, r1 simple, r2 compound, n]. Offer A wins on the five short entries, B on the five long ones. Source: original. */
L: [[60000,12,11,2],[60000,12,11,4],[45000,10,9,2],[45000,10,9,4],[150000,23/2,10,2],[150000,23/2,10,6],[27000,9,8,3],[27000,9,8,7],[90000,14,12,2],[90000,14,12,6]];
E: L[ix];
P: E[1]; r1: E[2]; r2: E[3]; n: E[4];
nm: ["Achieng","Kiprono","Wanjiru","Omondi","Nekesa","Mutua","Chebet","Barasa","Njeri","Hassan"][ix];
S: P*(1+r1*n/100);
C: P*(1+r2/100)^n;
ky: if S>C then 1 else 2;
nky: 3-ky;
m2: 1+r2/100;
/* diagnostics */
SI1: P*r1*n/100;
C1: P*(1+r1/100)^n;
S2: P*(1+r2*n/100);
Cm: P*(1+r2/100)^(n-1);
opt3: [[1, is(ky=1), "Offer A"], [2, is(ky=2), "Offer B"]];
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
